<title>GERMANY: Pan-German April adjusted jobless rises S/A 8,000.</title>
<headline>Pan-German April adjusted jobless rises S/A 8,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Apr 97	Mar 97	   Apr 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)		4.347 mln   4.477 mln	3.967 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		  4.299 mln   4.291 mln	3.918 mln</p>
<p> Change in adj number	+8,000	-25,000	  n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		  11.3 pct    11.7 pct	 10.4 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	  238,796     285,933	  390,407</p>
<p> Vacancies (unadj)	   363,261     372,001	  373,542</p>
<p> Change in numbers in work Feb 97	Jan 96</p>
<p>				  -72,000	-148,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
